  {
    "key": "lead.followup",
    "name": "Follow-up (AI-written)",
    "description": "LEAD_FOLLOWUP. The one playbook in this pack the model writes, because a follow-up has to respond to what the enquiry actually said \u2014 which is exactly the judgement a template cannot make and a human should therefore check. Ships isActive:false like every AI playbook (D59) \u2014 installing a pack must never be the moment a tenant starts sending model-written messages to strangers; POST /v1/playbooks/lead.followup/activate switches it on. Its data contract is the field list lead-message.service.ts read off the `lead_profiles` table (interests, inquiry_source, conversion_stage, last_interaction, metadata); there is no such table here, so the caller supplies them per event and anything durable lives on recipients.attributes (\u00a70.10 tiers 1 and 2). Every field is optional with a default, because the source read them all defensively.",
    "priority": 20,
    "isActive": false,
    "approvalPolicyKey": "lead.sales-review",
    "contentSource": {
      "kind": "ai",
      "promptPackKey": "lead.nurture",
      "goal": "Follow up on the enquiry with something useful and one easy-to-decline next step"
